   <dc:creator>
    <rdf:Seq>
     <rdf:li>-</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq>
   </dc:creator>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Protesters take part in the civil disobedience campaign, in June 1952, in Johannesburg, by occupying places for white people. The civil disobedience campaign against the apartheid regime of racial segregation was launched on 26 June 1952 by the ANC together with the South African Indian Congress (SAIC). It was conceived as a mass defiance campaign following the example of Mahatma Gandhi's passive resistance in Natal and India. More than 8,500 volunteers or 'defiers' deliberately violated oppressive laws, in non violent protests, strikes, boycotts, and marches, and were imprisoned for this peacefull actions. (Photo by - / AFP) (Photo by -/AFP via Getty Images)</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
